<title>USA: Top selling vehicles for first half of 1997.</title>
<headline>Top selling vehicles for first half of 1997.</headline>
<dateline>DETROIT 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following list is the top</p>
<p>20 best-selling vehicles for the first half of 1997, as</p>
<p>reported by individual automakers and compiled by Autodata</p>
<p>Corp.</p>
<p>    VEHICLE		   '97 YTD SALES   % CHANGE FROM '96</p>
<p> 1. Ford F-Series................383,353..............-7.1</p>
<p> 2. Chevrolet C/K Pickup.........265,891..............-1.5</p>
<p> 3. Toyota Camry.................206,486.............+15.7</p>
<p> 4. Ford Explorer................186,345..............-9.5</p>
<p> 5. Ford Taurus..................177,931..............-6.4</p>
<p> 6. Dodge Ram Pickup.............171,448.............-14.5</p>
<p> 7. Chevrolet Cavalier...........164,201.............+13.3</p>
<p> 8. Honda Accord.................161,045.............-12.4</p>
<p> 9. Honda Civic..................157,778..............+9.7</p>
<p>10. Dodge Caravan................153,358..............-3.0</p>
<p>11. Ford Escort..................149,587...............0.0</p>
<p>12. Ford Ranger Pickup...........147,438..............+0.1</p>
<p>13. Saturn.......................128,623..............-8.1</p>
<p>14. Chevrolet Lumina.............125,025.............-12.0</p>
<p>15. Jeep Grand Cherokee..........121,781..............-1.5</p>
<p>16. Toyota Corolla...............116,558.............+13.3</p>
<p>17. Ford Windstar................109,239..............+3.7</p>
<p>18. Ford Expedition..............107,080............+415.3</p>
<p>19. Chevrolet S Series Pickup....104,366..............+8.3</p>
<p>20. Pontiac Grand Am.............103,412.............-10.0</p>
</text>
